    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe HUAWEI command `isis enable 1` enables IS-IS on an interface with process ID 1. In Juniper:\\n1. IS-IS is enabled per interface under the protocols hierarchy\\n2. The interface names are slightly different (ge-1/0/0.0 for GigabitEthernet1/0/0 and lo0.0 for LoopBack0)\\n3. Juniper doesn't use process IDs in the same way, so we just enable IS-IS on the interfaces\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would typically also need global IS-IS configuration (level, NET, etc.) which corresponds to other parts of the Huawei configuration not shown in this specific translation.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe HUAWEI command `isis enable 1` enables IS-IS on an interface with process ID 1. In Juniper:\\n1. IS-IS is enabled per interface under the protocols hierarchy\\n2. The interface names are slightly different (ge-1/0/0.0 for GigabitEthernet1/0/0 and lo0.0 for LoopBack0)\\n3. Juniper doesn't use process IDs in the same way, so we just enable IS-IS on the interfaces\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would typically also need global IS-IS configuration (level, NET, etc.) which corresponds to other parts of the Huawei configuration not shown in this specific translation.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0'}]]": 1,
